**Quick answer:** An AI mock interview is a spoken practice interview with an AI interviewer based on a specific job and your resume. To get value from it, choose a real posting, answer out loud as if it were the real thing, read the feedback, rewrite your two weakest answers and try again. On GetHired you create a practice interview from a job and a resume, talk to the interviewer in your browser and get a written coaching report. Each session costs 5 AI credits.

Knowing an answer and saying it clearly are different skills. Reading question lists builds the first. Speaking out loud builds the second.

## How do you set up an AI mock interview?

1. Find the job on [GetHired](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/jobs) and copy the link to its page.
2. Open [Interviews](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/interview) and choose **Create Interview**.
3. Pick the resume you'd send for this role and paste the job link.
4. Start the session when you're somewhere quiet, with your microphone working.

You need a completed profile and enough AI credits. Credits are charged when a session starts, not when you create the interview. You can also ask the [agent](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/agent) to set one up for a job you're interested in.

## What feedback do you get after a mock interview?

{% table %}
-
- Part of the report
- What it tells you
---
- Overall feedback
- A short summary of how the session went
---
- Strengths
- What worked, with evidence from what you said
---
- Areas to improve
- What fell short, the evidence, and a suggestion
---
- Communication score
- 1 to 5, with the reason
---
- Role fit score
- 1 to 5, based on your answers and the role
---
- Practice tips
- What to work on next time
{% /table %}

The report is written to coach you. It isn't a hiring decision, and a high score doesn't promise an offer. Practice interviews are private: companies don't see them.

## How do you get the most out of a practice session?

### Treat it as real

Don't pause to look things up, and don't restart an answer halfway. You want to see how you perform under normal conditions.

### Prepare stories, not scripts

Have five or six examples from your own work ready: a hard bug, a disagreement, a deadline, a mistake, something you're proud of. The [STAR method](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/the-star-method-for-software-engineers-how-to-answer-behavioral-interview-questions) gives each one a clear shape.

### Say what you did

"We rebuilt the service" hides your part. Say "I designed the data model and ran the migration" if that's what happened.

### Give specifics

Name the constraint, the decision and the result. Specific answers are easier to believe and easier to follow up.

### Finish your answers

Many people trail off. End with the outcome or what you learned, then stop.

## How do you turn feedback into better answers?

1. **Pick the two most important improvement areas.** Fixing everything at once rarely works.
2. **Rewrite those answers as bullet points,** not full sentences.
3. **Say each one aloud** until it runs about one to two minutes without rambling.
4. **Run another session** for the same job.
5. **Compare the two reports.** Check whether the same weaknesses show up again.

## Which kinds of questions should you practise?

- **Introductions:** "Tell me about yourself."
- **Motivation:** why this company and this role.
- **Experience:** walk through a project on your resume.
- **Behavioural:** conflict, failure, leadership, tight deadlines.
- **Technical:** concepts and trade-offs you can explain by talking. See our [top 25 software engineer interview questions](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/top-25-software-engineer-interview-questions-and-how-to-answer-them).

A voice interview doesn't replace writing code or drawing a design. Practise those separately, for example with our [system design framework](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/system-design-interview-preparation-a-step-by-step-framework-for-2026).

## Is a practice interview the same as a company's AI screening interview?

No.

{% table %}
-
-
- Practice interview
- Company screening interview
---
- Who starts it
- You
- A company invites you after you apply
---
- Who sees the result
- Only you
- The hiring team
---
- Attempts
- Run another session whenever you like
- One attempt, plus one retry for a technical failure
---
- AI credits
- 5 per session
- None of your credits
{% /table %}

Practising first is a good way to get comfortable with speaking to a voice interviewer before one counts.

## Frequently asked questions

### Do AI mock interviews actually help?

They give you repetition and written feedback at any time of day, which helps you answer more clearly. They work best alongside real preparation: knowing your own experience and the company.

### Can companies see my practice interviews?

No. Your practice interviews are private.

### How much does a mock interview cost on GetHired?

Each practice session costs 5 AI credits, charged when the session starts.

### Can I practise for a job I found on another site?

Creating a practice interview needs a link to a job page on GetHired. Search GetHired for the same or a similar role.

### How many mock interviews should I do before a real one?

At least two for an important role, with time between them to improve the answers the first report flagged.

[Start practising with an AI interview](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/ai-interview) for a role you want.
